 "idea_credit": "jacksonxly (framing + staked standing); roots Biba 1977, Myers&Liskov DLM, CaMeL 2503.18813, Douceur 2002",
 "verdict": "EMPIRICAL on real LoCoMo (corrects the toy): corroboration-integrity is a WEAK poison signal, not none (AUROC 0.68 vs a naive transplant poison) and not a strong one — an adaptive poison that blends into the conversation would erode it toward chance. So the low-water-mark frontier is FAVORABLE but lossy (gap 0.27): at ~88% poison closure you still lose 74% of true-recall. Earned standing (orthogonal, from real earlier-session recurrence) refunds 0.38 of that, but 60% of real rare-true carry no standing (the irreducible cold-start tail). And the Sybil floor is a TRADEOFF: a 2-forgery poison (integrity ~0.70) passes at any tau below ~0.7 (100% at moderate closure) and is only blocked by a tau so high it destroys benign utility. RBAC gates the actor, IFC gates the data, membership-cost gates the identity — and cold start is the empirical price of the last one without a registrar."
